WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.959 line:80% size:94% align:center
Model config: three roles, one command,

00:00:02.959 --> 00:00:06.450 line:80% size:94% align:center
one page. Here's what changes, in build order.

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:09.534 line:80% size:94% align:center
First, one models contract: one table,

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:12.950 line:80% size:94% align:center
three roles. Orchestrator, builder, reviewer.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:16.476 line:80% size:94% align:center
The small builder and the fixer follow your builder,

00:00:16.476 --> 00:00:18.075 line:80% size:94% align:center
unless you override them.

00:00:18.275 --> 00:00:21.369 line:80% size:94% align:center
Then one command, openwiz models: show,

00:00:21.369 --> 00:00:24.225 line:80% size:94% align:center
list and set, for you or your agent.

00:00:24.425 --> 00:00:27.060 line:80% size:94% align:center
Set refuses a model you can't run,

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.850 line:80% size:94% align:center
and warns on a same-family reviewer.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:33.149 line:80% size:94% align:center
In the app, a Models page shows your roles.

00:00:33.149 --> 00:00:36.175 line:80% size:94% align:center
Change hands the exact line to your agent.

00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:39.694 line:80% size:94% align:center
Launch-fleet starts every agent from the table;

00:00:39.694 --> 00:00:42.025 line:80% size:94% align:center
setup writes it for new projects.

00:00:42.225 --> 00:00:45.647 line:80% size:94% align:center
Next, OpenWiz's fleet tick reads the table.

00:00:45.647 --> 00:00:47.875 line:80% size:94% align:center
Older projects keep working.

00:00:48.075 --> 00:00:50.867 line:80% size:94% align:center
Last, OpenWiz's own fleet moves over.

00:00:50.867 --> 00:00:53.281 line:80% size:94% align:center
New agents use a change at once;

00:00:53.281 --> 00:00:56.375 line:80% size:94% align:center
running agents finish on their old model.
